meta {
  name: 5 Set work hours
  type: http
  seq: 6
}
put {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/providers/{{providerEmail}}/work-hours
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "startHour": 8,
    "endHour": 17
  }
}
docs {
  The provider's own calendar day — the window `AvailabilityCalculator` generates bookable slots in. Whole
  hours on the provider's own clock (`timeZoneId`), and `endHour` is **exclusive**: 8–17 means the last
  session finishes at 17:00.

  A dedicated route rather than two more fields on `PUT /api/v1/providers/{email}`, because that one
  replaces the whole stored document. This one is a targeted `$set`, so saving hours cannot disturb the
  provider's services or appointments.

  A provider who has never called this is treated as 08:00–17:00.

  Answers:
  - `200` with the updated provider on success.
  - `400` when the window does not open before it closes (`startHour >= endHour`), or when either hour is
    out of range — `startHour` 0–23, `endHour` 1–24. Rejected, never clamped: a silently corrected window
    would leave the provider looking at hours they did not choose.
  - `403` for another provider's email. Ownership-guarded, and validation runs **before** the guard, so an
    invalid body gives `400` and never reaches it.
  - `404` when no provider has that email.

  Verify with `2 Get provider by email` — `workDayStartHour`/`workDayEndHour` come back on the entity, and
  the read's 5-minute cache is invalidated by this write.
}
